{{Han etym}}
{{liushu|p}} – a fruit (specifically a pomelo).

{{zh-ref|Wu and Shi (2022)}} notes that {{lang|zh|由}} was originally a component extracted from the oracle bone script of {{zh-l|*柚|pomelo}}, where it depicted the fruit itself. It was later used exclusively for phonetic loans, fully differentiating from {{zh-l|*柚}}. 

Traditional analysis in ''{{w|Shuowen}}'' interprets it as a container with a needle ({{zh-l|*十}}, original form of {{zh-l|*針}}). Alternatively, Tang Lan (唐蘭) interpreted it as the pictogram of a helmet (original character of {{zh-l|*冑}}). 

